    "faq": {
      "type":"suntneew-pdp-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q1":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"Which vehicles can KB700 support?","answer":"<p>KB700 is for compatible 12V vehicle batteries, with a documented reference of up to 6.0L gasoline or 4.0L diesel engines. Do not attempt to jump-start a higher-rated engine or a battery with a different voltage.</p>"}},
        "q2":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"What does up to 25 starts mean?","answer":"<p>The up-to-25-starts reference is based on the product documentation for a typical 1.5L passenger vehicle under a full charge. Results vary with engine size, battery condition, temperature and vehicle condition.</p>"}},
        "q3":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"How do I use KB700 to jump-start a vehicle?","answer":"<p>Charge the unit to at least 50%, insert the clamp plug, connect red to the positive terminal and black to the negative terminal, wait for the green indication, then start the vehicle. Remove the clamps within 30 seconds after the vehicle starts.</p>"}},
        "q4":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"What are the three air-duster speeds?","answer":"<p>The documented three levels are 30,000 RPM for up to 18 minutes, 70,000 RPM for up to 8 minutes and 100,000 RPM for up to 4.5 minutes. The maximum fan speed specification is 105,000 RPM (±10%).</p>"}},
        "q5":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"Can I charge a phone with KB700?","answer":"<p>Yes. The USB-A output supports emergency device charging at 5V/2A. Recharge KB700 through its Type-C input at 5V/2A; typical recharge time is about four hours.</p>"}},
        "q6":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"What light modes are available?","answer":"<p>The 2W LED has Steady, Flashing and SOS modes. Turn the unit on, then press the lighting key to move through the modes.</p>"}},
        "q7":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"Can I use KB700 in rain or rinse it clean?","answer":"<p>No. Keep the unit, clamps and ports dry. The product is not marketed as waterproof or IP rated; do not rinse, submerge or use it when wet.</p>"}}
      },
